					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{}0\\,\\end{dmath*}"
				}
			],
			"source": "chk:= @(comm) - 1/4 R_{\\mu\\nu}^{m n} \\Gamma_{m n} \\psi_{\\rho};\nsubstitute(chk, Rdef)\ndistribute(chk)\nsort_product(chk)\ncanonicalise(chk)\nrename_dummies(chk)\ncollect_terms(chk);"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 5014460475085604179,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 5014460475085604179,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "\\subsection*{The action}\n\nThe action is the sum of the Hilbert action $\\mathcal{L}^{(2)}$ and the Rarita-Schwinger action\n$\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$ (vN~1.7 eq.~(1)). We keep the two parts separate, so we can follow\nwhich terms in the variation cancel against which. In vN the Hilbert action is written\nas $-\\tfrac12 e\\, e^{a\\nu} e^{b\\mu} R_{\\mu\\nu ab}$:"
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "\\subsection*{The action}\n\nThe action is the sum of the Hilbert action $\\mathcal{L}^{(2)}$ and the Rarita-Schwinger action\n$\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$ (vN~1.7 eq.~(1)). We keep the two parts separate, so we can follow\nwhich terms in the variation cancel against which. In vN the Hilbert action is written\nas $-\\tfrac12 e\\, e^{a\\nu} e^{b\\mu} R_{\\mu\\nu ab}$:"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 3413071379190433056,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "input",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 14093620834036638934,
					"cell_origin": "server",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"cells": [
						{
							"cell_id": 13643373422215570643,
							"cell_origin": "server",
							"cell_type": "input_form",
							"source": " -  1/2 e e_{m}^{\\nu} e_{n}^{\\mu} R_{\\mu \\nu}^{m n}"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e e_{m}\\,^{\\nu} e_{n}\\,^{\\mu} R_{\\mu \\nu}\\,^{m n}\\end{dmath*}"
				}
			],
			"source": "L2:= -1/2 e e_{m}^{\\nu} e_{n}^{\\mu} R_{\\mu\\nu}^{m n};"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 1920814257899668885,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 1920814257899668885,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "vN writes the gravitino action as\n$-\\tfrac12\\epsilon^{\\mu\\nu\\rho\\sigma}\\bar\\psi_\\mu\\gamma_5\\gamma_\\nu D_\\rho\\psi_\\sigma$.\nIn four dimensions $\\epsilon^{\\mu\\nu\\rho\\sigma}\\gamma_5\\gamma_\\nu$ is proportional to\n$e\\,\\Gamma^{\\mu\\rho\\sigma}$, so we can write the action without $\\gamma_5$ or an epsilon\ntensor. The overall normalisation of this term relative to $\\mathcal{L}^{(2)}$ is checked\nlater, when the Einstein tensor terms of the two parts have to cancel.\nThe curved indices on the gamma matrix are converted to flat ones, so that the vielbeine\nappear explicitly and can be varied."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "vN writes the gravitino action as\n$-\\tfrac12\\epsilon^{\\mu\\nu\\rho\\sigma}\\bar\\psi_\\mu\\gamma_5\\gamma_\\nu D_\\rho\\psi_\\sigma$.\nIn four dimensions $\\epsilon^{\\mu\\nu\\rho\\sigma}\\gamma_5\\gamma_\\nu$ is proportional to\n$e\\,\\Gamma^{\\mu\\rho\\sigma}$, so we can write the action without $\\gamma_5$ or an epsilon\ntensor. The overall normalisation of this term relative to $\\mathcal{L}^{(2)}$ is checked\nlater, when the Einstein tensor terms of the two parts have to cancel.\nThe curved indices on the gamma matrix are converted to flat ones, so that the vielbeine\nappear explicitly and can be varied."
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 3279525101560688823,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "input",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 18006674744647041510,
					"cell_origin": "server",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"cells": [
						{
							"cell_id": 4760090410633266709,
							"cell_origin": "server",
							"cell_type": "input_form",
							"source": " -  1/2 e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{\\mu \\nu \\rho} D_{\\nu}(\\psi_{\\rho})"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{\\mu \\nu \\rho} D_{\\nu}{\\psi_{\\rho}}\\end{dmath*}"
				},
				{
					"cell_id": 2106567605808188612,
