		{
			"cell_id": 3049643550819926019,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 3049643550819926019,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "\\subsection*{The curvature terms}\n\nThere are now two kinds of terms: curvature terms, and terms containing $D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda$\n(the terms of vN~1.7 eq.~(9)). We zoom in on the curvature terms and simplify the gamma\nmatrix algebra. The terms with five gamma matrices vanish in four dimensions. To compare\nthe terms coming from the two gravitino variations, all spinor bilinears are written with\n$\\bar\\epsilon$ on the left, using the Majorana flip relations (vN~1.7 eq.~(5)).\nThe terms with three gamma matrices then cancel."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "\\subsection*{The curvature terms}\n\nThere are now two kinds of terms: curvature terms, and terms containing $D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda$\n(the terms of vN~1.7 eq.~(9)). We zoom in on the curvature terms and simplify the gamma\nmatrix algebra. The terms with five gamma matrices vanish in four dimensions. To compare\nthe terms coming from the two gravitino variations, all spinor bilinears are written with\n$\\bar\\epsilon$ on the left, using the Majorana flip relations (vN~1.7 eq.~(5)).\nThe terms with three gamma matrices then cancel."
		},
